# Travels WITH the bundle, so a consumer inherits the protection instead of having to remember it.
#
# The rules in the SDK repository's own .gitignore cannot help a consumer: they live in a different
# repository. And a bundle directory is where it matters most — a machine-local settings file in one
# of these once held a developer's allow-list, absolute paths into an unrelated repository and a curl
# command carrying DEV stand credentials, sitting one `cp -R` away from every consumer that installed
# the kit. Three .env files of the same kind did reach a shared remote and had their accounts rotated.
settings.local.json
scheduled_tasks.lock
.env*
.fetched-*

# Per-run state written by the hooks: an artefact of one session, never of the bundle.
.stand-test/
